The **Registration Data Access Protocol (RDAP)** provides access to information about Internet resources ([domain names](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domain_name), [autonomous system numbers](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autonomous_system_\(Internet\)), and [IP addresses](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IP_address)). Unlike [WHOIS](https://whois.icann.org/en/about-whois), which it replaces, RDAP provides:
  * Machine-readable representations of registration data;
  * Structured request and response semantics;
  * Differentiated access;
  * Internationalisation;
  * Extensibility.


**RDAP.org** provides a "bootstrap server", i.e. single end point for RDAP queries. RDAP.org aggregates information about all known RDAP servers. RDAP clients can send RDAP queries to RDAP.org, which will then redirect requests to the appropriate RDAP service.
